# Vendored third-party code (docs/internals/refs.md §6).

Every file below is byte-identical to the pinned upstream revision. Nothing here is
restyled, renamed or patched: a capability a vendored library lacks goes upstream, it is
not added locally. test/vendor_audit.py re-hashes this tree and fails the build on drift.

u_bstream is pinned at its tag v1.3.0, which carries the C99 guard on its 64-bit
accessors (__STDC_VERSION__ >= 199901L); v1.2.0 gated them on C11 and would drop them
under this tree's -std=c99. u_sstream is pinned at its tag v1.5.2, which carries the fix to
U_sstream_put_double for negative values in (-1, 0) and a 10_put_str test that
initialises its buffer, so the test passes in a Release build too.


